        "reply_text": "You can lodge a grievance through the National Consumer Helpline by visiting their web portal or calling their toll-free numbers, or you can file a complaint with the District Commission. The remedies and options depend on the facts and the authority's decision.\n\nKeep the bill and screenshots of your chats with company support ready as proof.\n\nWhat I understood: You bought a phone charger for a certain amount, it is defective, and company support is unresponsive.\n\nA product liability action may be brought by a complainant against a product manufacturer, service provider, or seller for any harm caused by a defective product.\n\nA product manufacturer is liable in a product liability action if the product contains a manufacturing defect, design defect, deviates from specifications, fails to conform to an express warranty, or lacks adequate instructions or warnings.\n\nYou can approach the National Consumer Helpline online at their web portal or by calling their toll-free numbers.\n\nYou may also file a complaint with the District Commission.\n\nPlease tell me the name of the company that made or sold the phone charger.\n\nSource: Department of Consumer Affairs - National Consumer Helpline (NCH), H NCH\nSource: Consumer Protection Act, 2019, section 35\nSource: Consumer Protection Act, 2019, section 83\nSource: Consumer Protection Act, 2019, section 84\n\nThis is legal information, not legal advice.",
